WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
By 2039, the world will look
and feel very different.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.360
The rate of change
is itself speeding up

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.800
and 20 years from now power
will have shifted dramatically.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.360
So who might be up and who might be
down, twenty years from now?

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.040
Let me take you on a journey
of possibles.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.640
Up, Africa.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.600
A rapidly increasing population

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.520
could fuel Africa's
surging economic growth.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.040
With a pool of young, better educated
and globally connected workers.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.560
But the biggest revolution in Africa

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.680
might be the spread of vast, super
arrays of far cheaper solar panels.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.680
To quote one energy guru...

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.400
Also up, China.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.320
THE superpower.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.360
After cornering many of the worlds
vital raw materials,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.760
could it now control both its own
people and many other countries

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.760
struggling to repay its loans.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.120
Could we see a world where China
exerts its influence

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.120
through movies and music too?

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.760
But if there are winners, which
countries could be losers by 2039?

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.280
Down, perhaps most of Europe.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.840
Financial services and banking will
be overwhelmingly driven by A.I.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.520
So Europe loses much of its
global edge.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.440
Parents who once urged children to
become lawyers and doctors,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.640
beg them to become
designers, artists, even actors.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.960
Anything creative -
not easily done by robots.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.880
Down but not out,
the United States of America.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.720
Eclipsed by China and paying a price
for getting late to wind and solar.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.160
Also down, the Middle East.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.480
Largely ignored internationally

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.200
because no one needs its
oil and gas anymore.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.280
Fossil fuels have become
the new forbidden fruit.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.320
Oil has lost most of its value,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.800
alternative fuels plus a collapse in
the use of plastics has seen to that.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.480
Water, clean water,
will be more precious than ever.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:04.320
Water wars have replaced oil wars,
along the Nile or any mighty river.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.240
Conflicts could break out
as states closest to the sea

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.520
fight those further upstream, accused
of taking too much of the water.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.000
Data however will be king.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.040
By 2039, more and more is being
bought and sold.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.200
Mostly illegally and in secret.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.520
All governments will rely on data as
THE method of control.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.720
Some countries will have followed
the Scandinavian lead.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:34.160
By choosing near total transparency -
of tax returns, earnings, lifestyles

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.600
to reduce the secret data threat.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.600
And more and more citizens everywhere
could be fighting back -

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.560
becoming data refuseniks.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.840
Fed up with the negative effects
of social media,

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.160
will they simply abandon
cyber space wherever they can?

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.400
Minimising their electronic footprint

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.920
even reverting to writing and
delivering private messages by hand.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:04.820
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

